{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`review_plan_start(ticket)` returns a `job_id`; callers then poll `gate_status(job_id)` and, when the job is terminal, read the retained `REVIEW_RESULT` findings for remediation. Today `gate_status` can report a plan-review run as terminal (`status: \"passed\"`, `verdict: \"BLOCK\"`) without giving the caller any per-run proof that the `REVIEW_RESULT` sidecar for that same run is the sidecar now readable from the tickets tracker. A caller that reads \"latest findings\" in that state can silently consume the previous run's findings.\n\nObserved 2026-09-01 while remediating `responsive-undamaged-auklet` (`549b-9cc5-940e-46c3`): job `1788326596882647223-94573cf0d90d404e87c74855306c16f2` reported terminal BLOCK, but the newest readable `REVIEW_RESULT` was `1788325963941841589-...-REVIEW_RESULT.json` from the prior run. The current run's sidecar appeared later as `1788327281362056852-...-REVIEW_RESULT.json`.\n\n## Root cause / actual layer\n\nThe in-process write order is not simply \"terminal index before `sidecar.emit()`\": `review_plan()` calls `sidecar.emit()` synchronously before `_mcp_llm._spawn_gate_daemon()` records the terminal `.rebar/gate_runs/<job_id>` entry in `finally`. The defect is the missing per-run sidecar receipt/generation in that terminal entry and status response:\n\n- `sidecar.emit()` is best-effort and returns only `sidecar_emitted: true|false` on the model verdict.\n- Before this fix, `_spawn_gate_daemon()` discarded that sidecar outcome when writing the terminal run index.\n- `gate_runs.gate_run_status()` reported terminal status from the local run index plus attestation currency only. For BLOCK verdicts the plan-review attestation is unsigned by definition, so the existing `durable` block cannot prove findings readability.\n- `sidecar.latest_review_result(ticket)` returns the newest usable sidecar for the ticket, not a sidecar tied to a specific `job_id` or review generation.\n\nTherefore any terminal run index without an exact sidecar receipt leaves the poller unable to distinguish: current sidecar readable, current sidecar not visible yet in this reader's tracker view, legacy/partial terminal index with unknown generation, or permanent best-effort sidecar failure. That ambiguity is the stale-read bug.\n\n## Fix plan\n\nMake the status contract explicit and additive; do not change verdict computation or make sidecar emission mandatory.\n\n1. When a plan-review sidecar is emitted, preserve existing return contracts while adding an exact write receipt:\n   - `_commands._seam.append_event()` keeps existing callers compatible: callers that ignored its old `None` return can still ignore it, while callers that need a receipt may read the returned event-envelope timestamp.\n   - `plan_review.sidecar.emit()` still returns `bool` for `sidecar_emitted` consumers, and additionally stamps `verdict[\"sidecar_reviewed_at\"]` with the exact ns timestamp returned by `append_event()` for the sidecar this review wrote.\n   - `plan_review.__init__` keeps `verdict[\"sidecar_emitted\"]` boolean semantics unchanged while carrying the stamped `sidecar_reviewed_at` on the same verdict.\n2. When an async plan-review daemon finishes, copy that exact completed-review receipt into the terminal run index: `sidecar_emitted:false` for permanent best-effort sidecar failure, or `sidecar_emitted:true` plus `sidecar_reviewed_at:<ns timestamp>` from the returned verdict.\n3. Extend `gate_status(job_id)` for plan-review jobs with a `findings` block:\n   - `sidecar_type: \"REVIEW_RESULT\"`\n   - `readable: bool`\n   - `reason: \"current-review-result-sidecar\" | \"review-result-sidecar-missing\" | \"sidecar-not-emitted\" | \"review-result-generation-unknown\" | \"run-<status>\"`\n   - `reviewed_at: int|null` (the expected sidecar timestamp for this run)\n   - `latest_reviewed_at: int|null` (the newest sidecar currently readable for this ticket)\n   - `job_started_at: int|null` only for legacy records with no receipt, for diagnostics.\n4. Mark `findings.readable=true` only when the exact `sidecar_reviewed_at` file exists and parses as a supported `plan_review_result_v1/v2` sidecar. Do not infer freshness from \"latest timestamp after job start\"; that could falsely attribute a later unrelated sidecar to a legacy job.\n5. Permanent failure disposition: if `sidecar_emitted` is false, `gate_status` still reports the terminal verdict but returns `findings.readable=false` and `reason=\"sidecar-not-emitted\"`. A poll-then-read caller must stop treating findings as pending and surface the unavailable findings condition instead of looping forever. `review-result-sidecar-missing` is a distinguishable not-readable state for an expected receipt that is not yet visible in this reader's tracker view; callers may poll it only under their normal bounded wait policy, but must never read latest findings while it remains false. `review-result-generation-unknown` is terminal-unavailable for legacy records with no receipt. `run-<status>` is emitted for non-terminal runs and means keep polling the run handle.\n\nThis honors the existing documented contract by making the missing state observable. It is not an API redesign: existing `status`, `verdict`, and `durable` semantics remain unchanged, and callers that ignore `findings` continue to work as before.\n\n## Scope / file impact\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/gate_runs.py`: compute and expose the plan-review findings-readability block from the run index and current tracker sidecar state.\n- `src/rebar/_commands/_seam.py`: return the event-envelope timestamp from `append_event()` as an additive receipt; existing callers can ignore it.\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sidecar.py`: keep `emit()` returning bool while stamping `sidecar_reviewed_at` on the verdict with the exact timestamp returned by `append_event()`.\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py`: verified call site; boolean `sidecar_emitted` semantics remain unchanged while the stamped receipt rides on the verdict.\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py`: record the exact per-run `REVIEW_RESULT` receipt from the completed review result in the terminal async gate index.\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py`, `src/rebar/_mcp_models.py`, and `src/rebar/schemas/plan_review_verdict.schema.json`: document/model the additive status and receipt fields.\n- `tests/unit/test_mcp_gate_async.py`: regression tests for the actual stale-read window and permanent sidecar failure disposition.\n- `AGENTS.md`, `docs/plan-review-gate.md`, `docs/mcp-reference.md`: document that plan-review pollers wait for `gate_status(job_id).findings.readable` before reading latest findings.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Reproduce the actual window with writer already returned: seed an old `REVIEW_RESULT`, record a terminal run index for a newer job with an expected `sidecar_reviewed_at`, do not create that sidecar yet, and assert `gate_status(job_id)` is terminal but `findings.readable=false` with `reason=\"review-result-sidecar-missing\"` and `latest_reviewed_at` pointing at the older sidecar.\n- [ ] After writing the expected current sidecar file, assert the same job reports `findings.readable=true`, `reason=\"current-review-result-sidecar\"`, and the expected `reviewed_at`.\n- [ ] Drive the documented poll-then-read sequence across two runs and assert it never returns the prior run's findings for the newer job; it returns no findings until the current job's exact sidecar is readable.\n- [ ] Assert permanent sidecar failure is distinguishable: a terminal plan-review run with `sidecar_emitted=false` reports `findings.readable=false` and `reason=\"sidecar-not-emitted\"`.\n- [ ] Assert the daemon records the exact sidecar receipt returned by `review_plan()` even when a newer same-ticket sidecar is already readable, so receipt capture cannot misattribute latest-by-ticket to this job.\n- [ ] Assert legacy terminal records without a per-run receipt report `findings.readable=false`, `reason=\"review-result-generation-unknown\"`, and expose `job_started_at` only as diagnostics.\n- [ ] Assert non-terminal plan-review runs report `findings.readable=false`, `reason=\"run-<status>\"`, and `reviewed_at=null`.\n- [ ] Validate with `pytest -q tests/unit/test_mcp_gate_async.py`, MCP schema coverage for the touched output model, `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and `make test`.\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- Changing when the plan-review verdict is computed or whether a BLOCK run is considered a completed (`passed`) gate run.\n- Making `REVIEW_RESULT` sidecars required for the verdict itself; sidecars remain best-effort observability.\n- Changing `plan_review_status` or signed-attestation currency.\n"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788362680453955001,"uuid":"0924e174-027a-49e8-addd-5a9844c0f682"}